{"translation-revision-date":"2026-10-31 19:27+0100","generator":"WP-CLI\/2.12.0","source":"build\/index.js","domain":"messages","locale_data":{"messages":{"":{"domain":"messages","lang":"hu_HU","plural-forms":"nplurals=2; plural=(n != 1);"},"Scan finished: new or modified administrators were found and an alert email was sent.":[""],"The test alert could not be sent \u2014 wp_mail() refused it. Check your SMTP plugin or hosting mail limits.":[""],"Test alert sent. If it does not arrive, the problem is your site mail configuration, not the firewall.":[""],"Scan finished: no new or modified administrators found.":[""],"Unknown":["Ismeretlen"],"%d alert could not be sent yet and will be retried on the next scan.":[""],"The last alert email could not be sent. Check your site mail configuration (SMTP plugin, hosting mail limits) \u2014 an alert that never arrives is no alert at all.":[""],"Unknown install error.":[""],"Status":["\u00c1llapot"],"Username":["Felhaszn\u00e1l\u00f3n\u00e9v"],"unknown":[""],"Two-factor login is on, but LW Firewall is not network-activated. On sites where the plugin is not active, people can still sign in with only a password, and that session is valid across the network. Network-activate LW Firewall to protect every site.":[""],"Loading\u2026":[""],"(opens in a new tab)":[""],"LW Plugins (opens in a new tab)":[""],"Try again":[""],"All":["Mind"],"Active":["Akt\u00edv"],"Inactive":["Inakt\u00edv"],"Not installed":[""],"Plugin":[""],"Settings saved.":[""],"Nothing was saved. Fix the highlighted fields and save again.":[""],"General":["\u00c1ltal\u00e1nos"],"General Settings":[""],"Protection":[""],"Spam":[""],"Blocked Bots":[""],"IP Rules":[""],"Geo Blocking":[""],"Security":[""],"Security Headers":[""],"Two-Factor":[""],"Two-Factor Login":[""],"Alerts":[""],"New Administrator Alert":[""],"Firewall Status":[""],"Logs":[""],"Request Logging":[""],"Import \/ Export":[""],"Has invalid fields":[""],"%d warning":[""],"LW Firewall home":[""],"LW Firewall sections":[""],"Documentation":[""],"Unsaved changes":[""],"Discard":[""],"Save changes":[""],"Set in wp-config.php":[""],"seconds":[""],"Alerts are turned off, so nothing was scanned. Enable alerts and save first.":[""],"Scan finished: new or modified administrators were found, but the alert email could not be sent yet. It is queued and retried on the next scan.":[""],"Check it now":[""],"Run the database scan immediately, or send a test message to the saved recipients.":[""],"Run scan now":[""],"Send test email":[""],"You have unsaved alert changes. The scan and the test email use the saved settings, so save first.":[""],"expired":[""],"Administrators tracked":[""],"Alerts go to":[""],"Snapshot taken":[""],"never \u2014 taken on the first scan":[""],"Next scan":[""],"not scheduled":[""],"%d entry":[""],"No country selected.":[""],"Not an ISO 3166\u20131 alpha-2 country code.":[""],"Remove %s":[""],"Search countries":[""],"Search a country or code\u2026":[""],"No country matches that search.":[""],"%d country blocked":[""],"List freshness":[""],"Stale":[""],"Current":[""],"Updated":[""],"Failed":[""],"Country IP lists":[""],"Next automatic update: %s":[""],"Without Cloudflare, visitors are matched against downloaded IPv4 and IPv6 lists per country.":[""],"Cloudflare detected: the CF-IPCountry header decides, so these lists are only a fallback.":[""],"Update CIDR Lists Now":[""],"Updating %1$d of %2$d\u2026":[""],"Save your changes first: the update downloads the lists of the saved countries.":[""],"Some lists could not be downloaded. The previous list is kept for those.":[""],"All country lists are up to date.":[""],"Country":[""],"Details":[""],"%d setting imported.":[""],"Settings missing from the file kept their current values.":[""],"Imported keys":[""],"Skipped, pinned in wp-config.php:":[""],"Unknown keys ignored:":[""],"%d value was invalid and not imported; that setting kept its current value:":[""],"Search":["Keres\u00e9s"],"Filter":[""],"Clear":[""],"Clear all filters":[""],"No entries match these filters.":[""],"Nothing here yet.":[""],"Previous page":[""],"Next page":[""],"Rows per page":[""],"Select all rows on this page":[""],"Clear selection":[""],"Bulk actions":[""],"%d result":[""],"Page %1$d of %2$d":[""],"Select: %s":[""],"%d selected":[""],"%1$d selected, %2$d on this page":[""],"applies to %1$d of %2$d":[""],"IPv6 \/64":[""],"Legacy entry":[""],"%s banned.":[""],"IP address":[""],"Duration (seconds)":[""],"Ban address":[""],"Locked usernames":[""],"Unlock all usernames":[""],"Locked":[""],"Expires":[""],"Actions":["M\u0171veletek"],"Enforced":[""],"Tracked only":[""],"Unlock":[""],"%d ban lifted. Its counters were cleared too, so the next request starts from zero.":[""],"All tracked bans lifted and their counters cleared.":[""],"%d ban could not be lifted:":[""],"Lift every ban and username lock, and clear the counters behind them? Addresses that keep attacking will be banned again by the rules.":[""],"Unlock %d username?":[""],"Unblock %d selected address and clear its counters?":[""],"Reason":[""],"Banned":[""],"Tracked but no longer enforced \u2014 the storage backend was cleared.":[""],"Unblock":[""],"Automatic Bans":[""],"Addresses the firewall banned on its own \u2014 brute-force lockouts, registration spam, password-reset floods and rate-limit escalation. Unblocking also clears the counters behind the ban, so the address starts from zero instead of being banned again on its next request.":[""],"Refresh":[""],"Enforced now":[""],"Expire within the hour":[""],"Ban store":[""],"Not enforced":[""],"Search banned IP addresses":[""],"No banned address matches that search.":[""],"No addresses are banned right now.":[""],"Bans appear here as soon as the firewall issues one.":[""],"Select all bans on this page":[""],"Unblock selected":[""],"Unblock every banned address":[""],"Blocked requests":[""],"Clear log":[""],"Logging is off, so no new blocked requests are recorded. Turn on \"Log blocked requests\" above and save.":[""],"Time":["Id\u0151"],"IP":[""],"User-Agent":[""],"URL":["URL"],"Search IP, URL or User-Agent":[""],"No log entries yet.":[""],"Log cleared.":[""],"Delete every log entry? This cannot be undone.":[""],"How long the ban lasts in seconds (3600 = 1 hour).":[""],"Username Lockout":[""],"Also counts failed logins per username, from every IP together, so an attacker rotating addresses is still stopped. A locked username cannot log in from anywhere until the lock expires; whitelisted IPs bypass it. Clear a lock from the Automatic Bans list on the IP Rules tab or with WP-CLI.":[""],"Lock usernames after repeated failed logins":[""],"Off":["Ki"],"Failed Attempts per Username":[""],"Number of failed logins for one username, from any IP, within the detection window above before that username is locked.":[""],"Username Lock Duration":[""],"How long the username stays locked, in seconds (900 = 15 minutes).":[""],"Spam Auto-Ban":[""],"Ban IPs that repeatedly send spam registrations, comments or reviews. A banned IP is blocked from the whole site, not just the form.":[""],"Ban Threshold":[""],"Number of rejected registrations, comments and reviews (counted together) from one IP before it is banned. A comment refused only because its form was too old is not counted.":[""],"Ban Duration":[""],"Comment & Review Protection":[""],"Stops bot comments and WooCommerce product reviews before they are stored, without a captcha. Works with every form built by comment_form(): classic and block themes, and both WooCommerce review forms. Administrators, editors of the post and whitelisted IPs are never checked.":[""],"Enable Comment Protection":[""],"Checks every comment and review sent through the comment form (wp-comments-post.php). Comments added through the REST API, XML-RPC or the admin are not affected.":[""],"Block bot comments and product reviews":[""],"Honeypot":["Honeypot"],"A hidden field that visitors and screen readers never see. Bots that fill every field are rejected. A form without the field (for example a hand-built theme form) is never rejected because of it.":[""],"Add a hidden honeypot field":[""],"Signed Form Token":[""],"Rejects comments posted straight to wp-comments-post.php without loading the page. If your theme builds its comment form without comment_form(), every comment is rejected: test a comment after turning this on.":[""],"Require a token from the rendered form":[""],"Minimum Fill Time":[""],"Reject comments sent faster than this many seconds after the page was generated.":[""],"Token Lifetime":[""],"How long a rendered comment form stays valid, in seconds (86400 = 1 day). Cached pages are safe: when a visitor starts typing into a form older than half this time, a fresh token is fetched in the background. Tokens are never single-use here, because a page cache shows the same form to everyone.":[""],"Registration Protection":[""],"Block bot sign-ups on wp-login.php?action=register without a captcha. Active only when \"Anyone can register\" is enabled in Settings \u2192 General.":[""],"\"Anyone can register\" is off on this site, so registration protection is idle until it is turned on.":[""],"Enable Registration Protection":[""],"Adds a signed proof-of-render token and honeypot to the registration form. Only active when \"Anyone can register\" is enabled.":[""],"Block bot registrations on wp-login.php?action=register":[""],"Catches generic bots that fill every field. Invisible to real users.":[""],"Single-Use Token":[""],"Stores used tokens in the firewall storage backend so each rendered form can register only once.":[""],"Reject reused tokens":[""],"Reject submissions faster than this many seconds after the form loaded (catches instant bot POSTs).":[""],"How long a rendered form stays valid, in seconds (3600 = 1 hour).":[""],"Password Reset Flood Protection":[""],"A reset flood has three shapes, and each needs its own limit: one IP hammering the form, many IPs targeting one person's inbox, and sheer volume burning your hosting mail quota.":[""],"Enable Reset Protection":[""],"Covers wp-login.php?action=lostpassword and the WooCommerce \"Lost your password?\" form \u2014 both go through the same WordPress hook. Requests started by an administrator or by WP-CLI are never limited.":[""],"Rate limit password reset requests":[""],"Requests per IP":[""],"How many reset requests one IP address may make per window. 0 disables this limit.":[""],"Per-IP Window":[""],"Length of the per-IP window in seconds (900 = 15 minutes).":[""],"Requests per Account":[""],"How many reset emails one account may receive per window, no matter how many different IPs ask. This is the only limit that stops a distributed flood of one person's inbox. 0 disables it.":[""],"Per-Account Window":[""],"Length of the per-account window in seconds (3600 = 1 hour).":[""],"Site-Wide Hourly Cap":[""],"Total reset emails the site will send in an hour. Protects your hosting mail quota and stops your domain being flagged as a spam source. 0 disables it.":[""],"Password Reset Hardening":[""],"Filter out direct bot POSTs, escalate repeat offenders to a site-wide ban, and optionally take administrator accounts out of the reset flow entirely.":[""],"Proof of Render":[""],"Rejects direct POSTs that never loaded the form. Only enforced on wp-login.php, since other lost-password forms (WooCommerce, custom login pages) do not render the token. Turn this off if a login plugin replaces the wp-login form.":[""],"Require a signed token and honeypot on the wp-login form":[""],"Reject submissions faster than this many seconds after the form loaded. Separate from the registration setting, so the two forms can be tuned independently.":[""],"How long a rendered lost-password form stays valid, in seconds (3600 = 1 hour).":[""],"Each rendered form may submit one reset request. Without this, a bot can load the form once and replay that token for the whole token lifetime.":[""],"Auto-Ban":[""],"A banned IP is blocked from the whole site by the MU-plugin worker. Account and site-wide limits never ban: they say nothing about who happened to ask last.":[""],"Ban IPs that trip the per-IP limit or fail the token check":[""],"Email Alert":[""],"Sends at most one message per limit per hour, to the recipients configured on the Alerts tab.":[""],"Email me when a reset limit is reached":[""],"Block Admin Resets":[""],"Closes the \"flood the admin inbox, then phish the reset link\" path entirely. A locked-out administrator can then only be recovered by WP-CLI or by another administrator, so leave this off unless you have that access.":[""],"Never allow password reset for administrator accounts":[""],"Yes":["Igen"],"No":["Nem"],"Country lists":[""],"Stale: no list younger than 7 days, so CIDR matching lets those visitors through.":[""],"Next automatic update":[""],"Cache directory writable":[""],".htaccess country block":[""],"Blocks by the Cloudflare CF-IPCountry header before WordPress loads.":[""],"No .htaccess file":[""],"Client IP detection":[""],"How the firewall sees your own request right now. Every visitor is identified the same way, so a wrong address here means shared rate-limit buckets and bans.":[""],"This address is not counted or banned: it is private, shared or one of your trusted proxies. Blacklist, whitelist, geo and bot checks still apply to it.":[""],"Detected IP":[""],"Taken from":[""],"Cloudflare header (CF-Connecting-IP)":[""],"Forwarded header from a trusted proxy":[""],"The connection itself (REMOTE_ADDR)":[""],"Forwarded headers":[""],"none":[""],"Trusted proxies configured":[""],"Trusted proxy match":[""],"Whether REMOTE_ADDR is one of the Trusted Proxies on the IP Rules tab.":[""],"Forwarded Header":[""],"Cloudflare detected":[""],"Routable":[""],"A private or reserved address means all visitors share one bucket.":[""],"Counted and bannable":[""],"Active Storage":[""],"Storage backend used for rate-limit counters.":[""],"Backend":[""],"Resolved backend":[""],"Configured":[""],"Round-trip test":[""],"Writes, reads and deletes a test value.":[""],"Working":[""],"Used by the File backend.":[""],"Versions":[""],"Worker":[""],"Matches the plugin":[""],"Mismatch \u2014 expected %s (will auto-update on next page load)":[""],"MU-Plugin Worker":[""],"The MU-plugin worker intercepts requests early, before themes and plugins load.":[""],"The worker was reinstalled.":[""],"Reinstall worker":[""],"Worker file":[""],"Installed":[""],"Worker Version":[""],"mu-plugins writable":[""],"No \u2014 make %s writable by the web server.":[""],"Last heartbeat":[""],"never":[""],"Kill switch":[""],"Last install attempt":[""],"Succeeded":[""],"Who Uses It":[""],"Users with an authenticator app or a passkey, per role.":[""],"With two-factor":[""],"of %d users":[""],"Passkeys":[""],"Available":[""],"Not available":[""],"This server or site address cannot use passkeys.":[""],"The PHP sodium and openssl extensions are required for two-factor login, and this server is missing at least one of them. Two-factor login stays off until they are enabled.":[""],"Role":["Szerepk\u00f6r"],"Users":[""],"Required":["K\u00f6telez\u0151"],"Large site: only the first accounts with a second factor were counted, so the numbers are a lower bound.":[""],"Required Roles":[""],"Users in these roles must set up a second factor. Until the grace period ends they only get a reminder; after that they are taken to the setup page at login instead of being locked out. Everyone else can opt in on their profile.":[""],"Core firewall settings \u2014 enable\/disable, storage backend, rate limits and WooCommerce filter protection.":[""],"Enable Firewall":[""],"Master switch \u2014 when off, the MU-plugin worker performs no checks (rate-limit, bot blocking, IP\/geo blocking, auto-ban all skipped).":[""],"Enable firewall protection":[""],"Storage Backend":[""],"Storage backend for rate-limit counters. Auto-detect tries APCu, then Redis, then file.":[""],"%s (not available on this server)":[""],"Rate Limit":[""],"Maximum number of rate-limited requests per IP within the time window. Applies to WooCommerce filters, login, REST, XML-RPC and any other protected endpoint.":[""],"Time Window":[""],"Time window in seconds for rate limiting.":[""],"Rate Limit Action":[""],"Response when the rate limit is exceeded. 302 strips query parameters and redirects to the same path; 429 returns a Retry-After header.":[""],"302 Redirect (strip filters)":[""],"429 Too Many Requests":[""],"WooCommerce Filters":[""],"WooCommerce product-filter URLs (filter_*, query_type_*, min_price, max_price, rating_filter and the Product Filters block arguments) are served only to visitors carrying a cookie that every page sets from JavaScript. Without it, a tiny page sets the cookie and reloads the same URL, so real visitors barely notice, while bot networks sending one request per IP never reach WooCommerce. Signed-in users and whitelisted IPs are not challenged. The per-IP rate limit above still applies to filter requests.":[""],"Require the visitor cookie for filter requests":[""],"Allow Googlebot":[""],"Let a genuine Googlebot (verified by reverse and forward DNS, cached for a day) request filter URLs without the cookie. Usually best left off: indexing filter combinations wastes crawl budget.":[""],"Skip the check for verified Googlebot":[""],"Add-to-Cart Links":[""],"Apply the same visitor-cookie check to GET links with ?add-to-cart= (each one creates a cart and a WooCommerce session). Real visitors get the product added after one quick reload. Add-to-cart forms and AJAX (POST) are never affected. The per-IP rate limit also applies while this is on.":[""],"Require the visitor cookie for add-to-cart links":[""],"Endpoint Protection":[""],"Enable rate limiting on specific WordPress endpoints.":[""],"Rate-limit wp-cron.php requests":[""],"Protects against DDoS attacks targeting wp-cron.php.":[""],"Rate-limit xmlrpc.php requests":[""],"Protects against brute-force and DDoS via xmlrpc.php.":[""],"Rate-limit wp-login.php requests":[""],"Rate-limits wp-login.php requests per IP.":[""],"Rate-limit REST API requests":[""],"Rate-limits \/wp-json\/ requests per IP.":[""],"Block 404 flood":[""],"Blocks IPs that generate excessive 404 errors (vulnerability scanning).":[""],"Brute-Force Login Protection":[""],"Ban IPs that submit too many failed login attempts (fail2ban style). A banned IP is blocked from the whole site, not just wp-login.php.":[""],"Enable Login Protection":[""],"Counts failed password attempts per IP via wp_login_failed.":[""],"Ban IPs after repeated failed logins":[""],"Failed Attempts":[""],"Number of failed login attempts before the IP is banned.":[""],"Detection Window":[""],"Seconds within which failed attempts are counted (600 = 10 minutes).":[""],"Automatically ban IPs that repeatedly exceed rate limits.":[""],"Enable Auto-Ban":[""],"After the threshold is reached, the IP is banned for the configured duration.":[""],"Ban IPs after repeated violations":[""],"Number of rate-limit violations before an IP is banned.":[""],"User-Agent strings to block (one per line, case-insensitive substring match).":[""],"Blocked User-Agents":[""],"User-Agent substrings (case-insensitive, one per line). Any request whose User-Agent contains one of these is blocked with 403.":[""],"Restore defaults":[""],"Manually allow or block IP addresses. Supports individual IPs and CIDR ranges (e.g. 192.168.1.0\/24).":[""],"IP Whitelist":[""],"IPs or CIDR ranges that bypass all firewall checks (one per line). Supports IPv4, IPv6, and CIDR notation (e.g. 10.0.0.0\/8, 2001:db8::\/32).":[""],"IP Blacklist":[""],"IPs or CIDR ranges blocked with 403 Forbidden before any other check (one per line). Supports IPv4, IPv6, and CIDR notation.":[""],"Reverse Proxy":[""],"Leave this empty unless the site sits behind a proxy or load balancer. A forwarded-for header is written by the client until the hop that set it is known, so trusting one without listing the proxies would let any visitor choose their own IP \u2014 and with it their own rate-limit bucket, ban status and country. Cloudflare is handled automatically and needs nothing here.":[""],"Trusted Proxies":[""],"IPs or CIDR ranges of your own proxies, one per line. On the common \"nginx in front of Apache on the same host\" layout this is 127.0.0.1 \u2014 without it every visitor arrives as 127.0.0.1 and shares a single bucket.":[""],"Read right to left, skipping hops that are themselves listed above. Only used when a trusted proxy is configured.":[""],"Block visitors from specific countries. Behind Cloudflare, the CF-IPCountry header is used (instant). Without Cloudflare, CIDR-based lookup is used (updated weekly).":[""],"Enable":["Enged\u00e9lyez\u00e9s"],"Enable Geo Blocking":[""],"Blocked Countries":[""],"Visitors from the selected countries are blocked with 403.":[""],"ISO 3166\u20131 alpha-2 country codes, one per line (e.g. IN, CN, RU).":[""],"Against MIME sniffing":[""],"The browser does not guess a file\u2019s type, so a text file can never run as JavaScript.":[""],"Against clickjacking":[""],"Other domains cannot embed your site in an iframe, so visitors cannot be tricked into clicking hidden elements.":[""],"Against URL leaks":[""],"Other sites only see your domain; the full URL, which may contain sensitive paths, stays on your site.":[""],"Against device access":[""],"Turns off the camera, microphone and geolocation, so even a compromised third-party script cannot ask for them.":[""],"All %d sent":[""],"Not sent":[""],"On":["Be"],"%d HTTP response headers the firewall adds to every page.":[""],"Set in wp-config.php (%s).":[""],"Two-factor login":[""],"After the password, users confirm with an authenticator app, a recovery code or a passkey. Passkeys can also replace the password.":[""],"Set network-wide on the main site.":[""],"These settings apply to the whole network: only a network administrator can change them.":[""],"Locked out? Add define( 'LW_FIREWALL_TWOFA_ENABLED', false ); to wp-config.php to switch two-factor login off at once, or remove one user's factors with wp lw-firewall 2fa reset <user>.":[""],"Grace Period":[""],"Days a required user can keep logging in with the password alone, with a reminder, before setup becomes mandatory.":[""],"Remember This Device":[""],"Days a browser can skip the second step after a successful one. 0 = off, every login asks.":[""],"Passwordless Passkey Login":[""],"Show a passkey button on the login page. A passkey replaces both the password and the second step.":[""],"Passkey button shown":[""],"Block Application Passwords":[""],"Application passwords skip the second step. Turn this on to disable them for users who have a second factor.":[""],"Disabled for these users":[""],"Allowed":[""],"Send an email whenever an account gains administrator privileges, or an existing administrator account is modified \u2014 no matter how it happened: the admin screens, a plugin, the REST API, WP-CLI, or a direct write into the database.":[""],"Enable Alerts":[""],"Works independently of the main firewall switch.":[""],"Email me when a new administrator appears":[""],"Notification Email":[""],"Separate multiple addresses with commas. Leave empty to use the site admin email.":[""],"Account Takeover":[""],"Watches the username, email address and password of every administrator. Rewriting an admin's email address is how an account is seized \u2014 it hands over the password reset flow while the user ID stays the same, so watching for new accounts alone would never see it.":[""],"Also alert when an existing administrator is modified":[""],"Database Scan":[""],"Compares the live administrator list against a stored snapshot. This is what catches accounts inserted straight into the database, created by code that bypasses the WordPress user API, or added while this plugin was inactive.":[""],"Hourly scan for administrators created outside WordPress":[""],"How detection works":[""],"WordPress hooks":[""],"Immediate. Catches every account creation or role change that goes through the WordPress user API \u2014 the Users screen, user registration, the REST API, WP-CLI, and any plugin or theme calling wp_insert_user() or set_role(). The alert names the acting user and their IP address.":[""],"Database scan":[""],"Within the hour. A snapshot of every administrator user ID is stored, and the scheduled scan diffs it against the live list. Anything that appears without a hook firing \u2014 a direct SQL INSERT, a modified wp_capabilities meta row, an account added while the plugin was off \u2014 shows up here and is flagged as created outside the normal WordPress flow.":[""],"What the snapshot stores":[""],"Per administrator: the user ID, the username, the email address, and a digest of the stored password hash. The digest only ever answers \"did this change?\" \u2014 the password itself is never stored, never compared and never printed in an alert.":[""],"No duplicate alerts":[""],"Both paths write to the same snapshot, so each event is reported exactly once. Existing administrators are recorded silently when the feature is turned on \u2014 you are only told about what happens afterwards. Removing an administrator is not reported; the account simply leaves the snapshot.":[""],"Firewall off":[""],"No problems found. The worker, storage and client IP detection all look healthy.":[""],"Enable Logging":[""],"Stores the last 100 blocked requests in the database.":[""],"Log blocked requests":[""],"Export Settings":[""],"Download your current firewall settings as a JSON file. You can use this file to import settings on another site.":[""],"Import Settings":[""],"Upload a previously exported JSON file. Valid settings in the file replace the current ones, invalid values are skipped and reported, and settings missing from the file keep their current values.":[""],"The file is larger than 256 KB, the most an import accepts.":[""],"The file does not contain valid JSON.":[""],"Settings imported, but some values were rejected.":[""],"Settings imported successfully.":[""],"Import":[""],"Import the settings from %s? Every valid setting in the file replaces the current value right away; invalid ones are skipped and listed afterwards.":[""],"Your unsaved changes on the other tabs will be discarded.":[""]}}}